        "summary": "Dy4 defect-dicubane SMM. χT at 300 K is 53.21 cm3 K mol−1; χT decreases to 46.37 cm3 K mol−1 at 13 K then rises to 62.32 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.8 K, indicating intramolecular ferromagnetic coupling dominated by dipolar interactions. Only 3 of the series shows slow magnetic relaxation. Frequency-dependent ac susceptibility below 10 K; Arrhenius barrier Δ = 3.7 K and τ0 = 4.8×10−5 s (zero dc field), and Δ = 4.9 K, τ0 = 3.0×10−5 s under 500 Oe. Cole–Cole α = 0.04–0.07. Relaxation rate 1/τ decreases from 520 Hz (zero field) to 430 Hz at 500 Oe, consistent with QTM.",
